## ⚠️ updated from the last document  — `service/EmployeeService.java` DOES need a change

The three controllers below all call `service.findByCode(username)` / `employeeService.findByCode(username)`. That method **does not exist** in your current `EmployeeService.java` — it only has `verify(code, name, role)` and `verifyAny(code, name)`, both of which require a name to match too. Without adding `findByCode`, the project won't compile.

Add this method to the class (it's a direct lookup by primary key, since `employeeCode` is `@Id` on `Employee`):

```java
public Optional<Employee> findByCode(String employeeCode){
    if(employeeCode == null || employeeCode.isBlank()){
        return Optional.empty();
    }
    return repository.findById(employeeCode.trim());
}
```

Add it right after `verifyAny(...)`, before the closing brace of the class. No import changes needed — `Optional` and `Employee` are already imported.

