## `controller/EmployeeController.java`

Find:
```java
@GetMapping("/auto-detect")
public ResponseEntity<Employee> autoDetect(HttpServletRequest request) {
    Optional<Employee> employee = workstationService.resolveByIp(request.getRemoteAddr());
    return employee.map(ResponseEntity::ok).orElseGet(() -> ResponseEntity.notFound().build());
}
```
Replace with:
```java
@GetMapping("/auto-detect")
public ResponseEntity<Employee> autoDetect(@RequestHeader(value = "X-Remote-User", required = false) String remoteUser) {
    if (remoteUser == null || remoteUser.isBlank()) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(401).build();
    }
    String username = stripDomainPrefix(remoteUser);
    Optional<Employee> employee = service.findByCode(username);
    return employee.map(ResponseEntity::ok).orElseGet(() -> ResponseEntity.notFound().build());
}

private String stripDomainPrefix(String remoteUser) {
    // IIS typically passes "DOMAIN\username" — keep just the username part.
    int backslash = remoteUser.indexOf('\\');
    return backslash >= 0 ? remoteUser.substring(backslash + 1) : remoteUser;
}
```
Also remove: the `WorkstationService` import, constructor parameter, and field from this file. Add `import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestHeader;`.

